  "notes": "Compatible patch release carrying the accepted runtime-inert descriptor lookup and pure settings-value coercion foundation for issue #433. Exact undeclared paths preserve their original request object, while descriptor-owned settings paths copy the input, canonicalize finite numeric values, require strict booleans and closed enum members, enforce finite inclusive bounds, preserve unknown keys for existing handler allowlists, and use non-reflecting validation diagnostics. The router does not call the helper, so request handling, persisted state, frozen API v1 behavior, gameplay, browser surfaces, and Admin remain unchanged. No database schema, production workflow, deployment route, provider, DNS, billing, public signup, live OAuth, mail, invitation, unrestricted public exposure, credential, or SSH-ingress behavior changes. The exact immutable v0.9.5.23 release remains the application-only predecessor, MySQL schema 2 remains exact, and database rollback is prohibited."
